    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\overrightarrow{AB}=\\overrightarrow{DC}$ and $\\overrightarrow{AD}=\\overrightarrow{BC}$.",
      "worked": "Opposite sides of a parallelogram have equal lengths. The vectors $\\overrightarrow{AB}$ and $\\overrightarrow{DC}$ also have the same direction, as do $\\overrightarrow{AD}$ and $\\overrightarrow{BC}$, so these two statements are true.\n\n$\\overrightarrow{BC}=-\\overrightarrow{DA}$, so the second statement is false. Also, $\\overrightarrow{AC}=a+b$ whereas $\\overrightarrow{DB}=a-b$, so the fourth statement is false.",
